{"ts": "2026-05-05T10:30:32.179703+00:00", "page_id": "p0044", "scope": "footnote", "target_id": "p0044_fn_002", "field": "notes", "before": "", "after": "Citation for Persons first, then a cross-reference via \"Vid.\" to Pontanus's history of Guelders. The pairing is interesting — Ussher is pointing to a corroborating discussion elsewhere.", "reviewer": "Paul Boys"}
{"ts": "2026-05-05T10:30:32.179703+00:00", "page_id": "p0044", "scope": "footnote", "target_id": "p0044_fn_002", "field": "review_status", "before": "draft", "after": "locked", "reviewer": "Paul Boys"}
{"ts": "2026-05-05T10:30:32.179703+00:00", "page_id": "p0044", "scope": "footnote", "target_id": "p0044_fn_003", "field": "text_gold", "before": "Martial. lib. 11. epigram. 4.", "after": "Martial. lib. 11. epigram. 4.\n\nEt qui purpureis jam tertia nomina fastis,\nIane, refers Nervæ.\n\nTrajanus vero post adoptionem, Nerva etiam dictus est: ut apud Ælianum, in\nTacticorum proœmio ad Hadrian. Imp. Ἐπεὶ δὲ τῷ Θεῷ πατρί σου Νέρουᾳ\nσυμβαλὼν, &c.", "reviewer": "Paul Boys"}
{"ts": "2026-05-05T10:30:32.179703+00:00", "page_id": "p0044", "scope": "footnote", "target_id": "p0044_fn_003", "field": "kind", "before": "citation", "after": "other", "reviewer": "Paul Boys"}
{"ts": "2026-05-05T10:30:32.179703+00:00", "page_id": "p0044", "scope": "footnote", "target_id": "p0044_fn_003", "field": "notes", "before": "", "after": "The whole thing is footnote q:  Citation — Martial. lib. 11. epigram. 4 Quotation — the actual couplet (Et qui purpureis jam tertia nomina fastis / Iane, refers Nervæ) Historical gloss — explaining that Trajan was also called Nerva after adoption Supporting citation — Aelian's Tactics in Greek as proof  It's one continuous note, moving from source location to quoted evidence to interpretive argument. I was wrong to treat it as a separate unnumbered item — the verse and the Aelian discussion are all part of q's apparatus, building the chronological case about Martial's dating.", "reviewer": "Paul Boys"}
